{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1171643-staking-a-werewolf","id":1171643,"title":"Staking a Werewolf","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-12-29T15:25:02-08:00","id":1171643,"title":"Staking a Werewolf","content":"I want to know if staking a werewolf through the heart will kill it. <br /> <br /> I understand that werewolves with low harmony can shift to Gauru form as a reflexive action, how does this affect the outcome?<br /> <br /> Is it a matter of the damage to the heart being greater than the werewolf's stamina?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4812-karhu_fueryon","name":"karhu_fueryon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4812_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-29T16:10:14-08:00","id":1171661,"title":"","content":"<b>RE: Staking a Werewolf</b><br /> <br /> In the Chronicles of Darkness combat system, called shots never really enhance lethality. The system already assumes that in most combat with weapons involved, you are already actively trying to kill your opponent. Regardless of where you are aiming your attack, the lethality will be based on how well the blow landed (ie. the number of successes plus weapon modifier). Driving a stake through someone's heart and getting any result other than &quot;severe and/or fatal injury' tends side case specific to creatures that don't need a working heart to live.<br /> <br /> Now that being said, a Storyteller can play the scene a few different ways. I personally like the Vampire Hunter stabbing a Werewolf in the heart but only inflicting 2-3 pointsof damage, in which case the Werewolf pulls the implement from their chest with an an understated &quot;Ow&quot; and begins to transform.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-29T16:32:32-08:00","id":1171664,"title":"","content":"Staking a heart takes a -3 roll, and you need to do 5 damage to actually pull it off. The end result is doing (at least) 5 damage. If it's a vampire, they're also knocked into torpor unless they have a special method of avoiding that bane, but werewolves don't really suffer from that weakness. For a werewolf, they take 5 damage. You could potentially do more, if you had a really nice roll, but you would need to do so much Lethal damage that it fills all their Lethal and Aggravated health boxes. That's how you would kill a human with a stake, too.<br /> <br /> You need 4-6 Harmony to shift to gauru reflexively for free. At 7-8 and 2-3 you can spend a point of Essence to reflexively do it, as well and at 0-1 you would probably just reflexively go gauru without any player input. Gauru form regenerates all Bashing and Lethal per turn so you would regenerate that damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-29T17:11:08-08:00","id":1171674,"title":"","content":"I did 15L with the stake to that heart. We wanted to know if It killed the thing or if he would just regenerate &gt;.&gt; Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-29T17:24:42-08:00","id":1171677,"title":"","content":"That's a big dicepool, from there it would depend if they had 7 or less Health.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-29T17:26:59-08:00","id":1171678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1171643-staking-a-werewolf?p=1171677#post1171677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a big dicepool, from there it would depend if they had 7 or less Health.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I dont know the health, but I am going to guess it's more than 7.. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And yes. Huge dice pool.<br /> <br /> Also: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1171643-staking-a-werewolf?p=1171664#post1171664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Staking a heart takes a -3 roll, and you need to do 5 damage to actually pull it off. The end result is doing (at least) 5 damage. If it's a vampire, they're also knocked into torpor unless they have a special method of avoiding that bane, but werewolves don't really suffer from that weakness. For a werewolf, they take 5 damage. You could potentially do more, if you had a really nice roll, but you would need to do so much Lethal damage that it fills all their Lethal and Aggravated health boxes. That's how you would kill a human with a stake, too.</div> </div> </div> </div> I thought everyone suffered from the weakness of needing their heart. Kind of die when something gets rammed through it. ^.^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 12-29-2017, 08:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-29T17:31:04-08:00","id":1171683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1171643-staking-a-werewolf?p=1171678#post1171678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought everyone suffered from the weakness of needing their heart. Kind of die when something gets rammed through it. ^.^</div> </div> </div> </div>Poking it isn't necessarily getting rid of it, and vampires just fall to torpor (though in character people might not know that, since torpor does look like death).<br /> <br /> It probably would have killed my werewolf but he was sort of a weakling from a combat standpoint.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-29-2017, 08:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-29T17:50:36-08:00","id":1171687,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the advice everyone !","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-30T02:57:46-08:00","id":1171757,"title":"","content":"There are no instant death hits. The rules are specifically made for vampire so they're the only ones that are affected in any way. I wouldn't apply those rules in any other gameline since then you end up with the possibility of piercing someone's heart (even regular humans) without not even causing full lethal to someone who really should be rapidly dying. Werewolves, just like anyone else, dies at full aggravated. If you didn't fill that werewolf's health track with aggravated damage, they'll just keep on rolling. (But at 15 lethal you probably made some aggravated due to roll over, so next hit, if as powerful, could very well kill the werewolf from damage alone.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T01:27:06-08:00","id":1171971,"title":"","content":"A stake through the heart with an exceptional success would also cause stun and bleeding tilts, not to mention a -5 penalty to all rolls just to stay awake, maybe not an insta kill in the case of a werewolf with 10 health in hishu but would give a huge ouch and death rage that woust still leave upon him a 5 aggravated damage wound that would take a long time to heal. Also werewolves don't bleed out easily, even unconcious they spend essence to heal lethal which can be more than one damage per round.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12906,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","user":"Story Letter","date":". 12-31-2017, 04:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T01:45:54-08:00","id":1171975,"title":"","content":"I can't remember if werewolves have to roll to stay awake, but the damage would only be lethal; not aggravated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T02:21:03-08:00","id":1171979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1171643-staking-a-werewolf?p=1171975#post1171975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't remember if werewolves have to roll to stay awake, but the damage would only be lethal; not aggravated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. Regeneration happens before they need to roll to remain conscious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T03:11:12-08:00","id":1171982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1171643-staking-a-werewolf?p=1171975#post1171975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't remember if werewolves have to roll to stay awake, but the damage would only be lethal; not aggravated.</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends on the story teller, on how he handles regeneration on initiative roster .<br /> <br /> If the werewolf plays first and takes damage that would knock him off, in the next round, assuming he plays first, will regenerate first and will ignore the consciousness roll later, since regeneration is reflexive and always happens in the start of a werewolf's turn, while the stamina roll comes right before a character takes an action in order to see if the character can act at all in the same round.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">If the werewolf plays last and takes damage that would knock him off, then he simply regenerates and ignores the consciousness roll and he plays his turn.<br /> <br /> Now if you rule that the consciousness roll happens before regeneration then simply in both cases at the beginning of his turn, no matter if he plays on the same turn or the next one, will roll to stay awake with the imposed penalties (if any) and if he stays awake then regenerate and take an action if able. If the werewolf fails to stay awake then he still regenerates and automatically wakes up, even though knocked down.<br /> <br /> Werewolves are falling unconscious and bleeding if they are full with lethal, except if they spend essence to heal or regenerate, or both.<br /> <br /> I am supporting the idea that shapeshifting and regeneration happen before consciousness roll, but thats a personal taking.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12906,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","user":"Story Letter","date":". 12-31-2017, 12:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T07:46:01-08:00","id":1171997,"title":"","content":"Unconsciousness rolls also happen at the start of a character's turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T09:49:29-08:00","id":1172019,"title":"","content":"Then do consciousness rolls and regeneration count simultaneously and get confused on what should happen first.<br /> The easy solution in order to keep the game smooth is to take in consideration what game you play, since its obviously a non werewolf game with a werewolf encounter and the story teller wants to keep the encounter difficult he will regenerate the wounds before the roll. If not then he will knock the werewolf down, since its lethal damage.<br /> <br /> A 1st edition rule though is that shapeshifting regeneration and consciousness rolls to happened in such an order that would allow the werewolf up to fighting shape for the longest time possible. So a regeneration can easily be the reaction that fights back the need to struggle for consciousness.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T11:20:12-08:00","id":1172032,"title":"","content":"I'm not arguing with you, SL.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T13:50:01-08:00","id":1172063,"title":"","content":"Wait, wait, wait... are we talking about &quot;staking&quot; a werewolf in the heart with silver? Or a vampire-style wooden stake?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T15:33:25-08:00","id":1172085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knowbody</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1171643-staking-a-werewolf?p=1172063#post1172063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, wait, wait... are we talking about &quot;staking&quot; a werewolf in the heart with silver? Or a vampire-style wooden stake?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think he means with wood or iron spear.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T15:50:50-08:00","id":1172090,"title":"","content":"Given the high dicepool I figured it involved a werewolf that was, for some reason, thought to be a vampire. So it was laying asleep and a wooden stake was stabbed at it.<br /> <br /> Something like Cold Embrace allows werewolves to seem dead, and since it doesn't immobilize them one can masquerade as a vampire, though they do get a bit of a penalty to move unless they're very Cunning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T18:44:20-08:00","id":1172125,"title":"","content":"~It\u2019s a cross over game~<br /> <br /> My vampire ( with 10 BP and vigor allowed for an insanely huge dice pool + autodamage) wanted to stake the werewolf in hopes it would down the damn thing before it got nasty. <br /> <br /> The werewolf had 10 life, give or take, he shifted as a reflexive action and regenerated the lethal it could, some was aggravated, so it stayed. <br /> <br /> My character asked for a silver stake, but that\u2019s when he ( in game ) found out he had a bane to silver. Unfortunately the stake was wood, since he uses it to stake vampires sometimes. It\u2019s what he had. <br /> <br /> -Sigh- both the baddies got away. And my vampire is left hunting them still.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 12-31-2017, 09:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-31T18:51:33-08:00","id":1172127,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry they got away, but thank you for the closure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T03:33:01-08:00","id":1172222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1171643-staking-a-werewolf?p=1172125#post1172125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">~It\u2019s a cross over game~<br /> <br /> My vampire ( with 10 BP and vigor allowed for an insanely huge dice pool + autodamage) wanted to stake the werewolf in hopes it would down the damn thing before it got nasty.<br /> <br /> The werewolf had 10 life, give or take, he shifted as a reflexive action and regenerated the lethal it could, some was aggravated, so it stayed.<br /> <br /> My character asked for a silver stake, but that\u2019s when he ( in game ) found out he had a bane to silver. Unfortunately the stake was wood, since he uses it to stake vampires sometimes. It\u2019s what he had.<br /> <br /> -Sigh- both the baddies got away. And my vampire is left hunting them still.</div> </div> </div> </div>10 blood points ? WUUUAAA<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />AAAUUUW !!!<br /> <br /> Elder Campaign ? Nice plot twist with the silver bane <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T14:34:16-08:00","id":1172387,"title":"","content":"Actually he is a serial Diablerist who eats bad guys. Like really bad. Bad guys. They call him the Blue Devil so he goes and collects souls to drag to hell. ( he has blue hair and is probably only 2 vampire years old. ) <br /> <br /> Just diablerized a whole lot. Story teller ( OP ) has been nice enough to let me diablerize supernaturals not just vampires. We made a blood line for it when he got to BP 6. <br /> <br /> The vampire he was hunting contracted the local werewolf pack to help.. both the alpha and the vampire got away when he started nomming down distractions &gt;.&gt; yay addictions.. lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T11:58:22-08:00","id":1172702,"title":"","content":"Hahahahaha god that you have fun, no a stake to the heart will not kill a werewolf but will put hm out of sight for a long time, around 20 days, and at kuruth edge, you may have chance to track him down if he snaps and makes some kills. You may recognise him from his blood, blood is always the answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-10T06:02:06-08:00","id":1174839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1171643-staking-a-werewolf?p=1172125#post1172125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">~It\u2019s a cross over game~<br /> <br /> My vampire ( with 10 BP and vigor allowed for an insanely huge dice pool + autodamage) wanted to stake the werewolf in hopes it would down the damn thing before it got nasty.<br /> <br /> The werewolf had 10 life, give or take, he shifted as a reflexive action and regenerated the lethal it could, some was aggravated, so it stayed.<br /> <br /> My character asked for a silver stake, but that\u2019s when he ( in game ) found out he had a bane to silver. Unfortunately the stake was wood, since he uses it to stake vampires sometimes. It\u2019s what he had.<br /> <br /> -Sigh- both the baddies got away. And my vampire is left hunting them still.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm curious, how were u able to avoid his kuruth and then fight him in Gauru form? Did he ran away while he was raging?<br /> <br /> anyway u were lucky! in my experierence with crossover games if a gauru falls into rage then either u kill him or disable him in some way or u have to run away and hope his pack won't hunt you down..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4247-lasombra","name":"Lasombra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-10T06:52:30-08:00","id":1174859,"title":"","content":"My vampire wasn't the only one there, nor was this werewolf. There were hunters, vampires and the werewolf's pack. Some of the vampires and wolfs were together and my vampire and some of the hunters were together. The baddies brought in a chopper and was sort of raining fire down on the lot. So I staked the wolf and flew up to deal with the chopper so some of the hunters ( humans ) wouldnt get shot to shit. That's when the wolf decided it would be a good time to leave the fight and set up an ambush when they were not on the losing end...<br /> <br /> Also a 10 BP vampire in a frenzy is a formidable foe for a werewolf in his deathrage. Eventually, the wolf was tracked down and killed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-10T10:46:57-08:00","id":1174917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1171643-staking-a-werewolf?p=1174859#post1174859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also a 10 BP vampire in a frenzy is a formidable foe for a werewolf in his deathrage. Eventually, the wolf was tracked down and killed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only that a vampire in frenzy cannot make sophisticated attacks like targetting specific body areas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12906,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","user":"Story Letter","date":". 01-10-2018, 01:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-10T11:50:56-08:00","id":1174932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1171643-staking-a-werewolf?p=1174917#post1174917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Only that a vampire in frenzy cannot make sophisticated attacks like targetting specific body areas.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm not exactly sure what you're trying to say there. I will hold off on any sort of response until I know the intent of your statement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-10T12:10:18-08:00","id":1174937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1171643-staking-a-werewolf?p=1174917#post1174917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only that a vampire in frenzy cannot make sophisticated attacks like targetting specific body areas.</div> </div> </div> </div>A vampire in frenzy isn't stupid. It's animalistic and monomaniacal, but not mindless. As the book says: &quot;the Beast isn\u2019t stupid.&quot; If the Beast believes staking is the best course of action to achieve its goal, then it will do so.<br /> <br /> Edit: I'm personally not surprised that a vampire beat a werewolf at those power levels. Werewolves start out hard with the regeneration, but vampires can become ridiculously dangerous with Vigor/Resilience, a giant bonus to all physical rolls in Frenzy, as well as being able to gain enormous dice pools with Physical Intensity. I play in a similarly high end game of VtR, and if you don't have 40+ dice on an attack then you're not even trying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 01-10-2018, 03:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-11T07:17:18-08:00","id":1175161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1171643-staking-a-werewolf?p=1174932#post1174932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'm not exactly sure what you're trying to say there. I will hold off on any sort of response until I know the intent of your statement.</div> </div> </div> </div><i><b>''That said, the Beast isn\u2019t stupid. It\u2019s capable of doing the kinds of things an enraged, terrified, or starving animal predator is''<br /> <br /> ''While frenzied, the vampire does everything in her power to accomplish the Beast\u2019s desires. She does so with immediate, forceful, and destructive abandon''</b></i><br /> <br /> <i><b>''the vampire risks losing control of her Beast.''</b></i><br /> <br /> The conclusions are yours.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12906,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","user":"Story Letter","date":". 01-11-2018, 10:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-11T07:22:26-08:00","id":1175162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1171643-staking-a-werewolf?p=1174937#post1174937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A vampire in frenzy isn't stupid. It's animalistic and monomaniacal, but not mindless. As the book says: &quot;the Beast isn\u2019t stupid.&quot; If the Beast believes staking is the best course of action to achieve its goal, then it will do so.</div> </div> </div> </div><i><b>''enraged, terrified, or starving animal predator''</b></i><br /> <br /> Sorry but the staking through the heart in frenzy is too sophisticated and more of metagame thinking rather than original frenzy reaction. Now if your Story Teller allows it and you have fun with it, I pass.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-11T08:23:15-08:00","id":1175178,"title":"","content":"I think Vitalis was saying that the staking and frenzying took place at different times.<br /> <br /> The first time, his character used a stake and failed. The frenzying came up during the rematch, when likely it wasn't attempting the stake again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-11T09:03:02-08:00","id":1175187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1171643-staking-a-werewolf?p=1175178#post1175178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Vitalis was saying that the staking and frenzying took place at different times.<br /> <br /> The first time, his character used a stake and failed. The frenzying came up during the rematch, when likely it wasn't attempting the stake again.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes. Thank you Nofather. That is exactly what happened. All fangs and claws the second time around. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> While I agree that staking something in the heart might be too much of a though for an enraged beast.. Stabbing something repeatedly in the chest with that stake might not be especially if you had the stake in your hand when you went into a rage. (as a matter of fact, that is portrayed many times in a blind rage.) I also think that some called shots are perfectly acceptable in a frenzy. If someone has a particularly deadly weapon in their hand, you might want to target their hand or arm to break it to make them drop it before they kill you with it. Self preservation is pretty high up there even when you are in a kill frenzy. <br /> <br /> For example, a vampire fighting against someone with a can of hair spray and a lighter. They might want to make them drop one of those things before they suddenly get set on fire. It would definitely put a damper on you trying to eat them...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-11T09:37:14-08:00","id":1175197,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2308_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2308\" data-vbnamecard=\"2308\">Vitalis</a> of course you will attack with your stick while in frenzy, but if I was your ST and since you have so high a BP, I would opt to keep things spicy with chances that may include. random called shots, a broken stick after a few blows, even after one blow (you are too strong for your own good), or even worse a stick brocken in your awesomely powerful grip, well wood cannot stand a supergrip of that magnitute, let the power of chance decide <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> But thats just the humble little me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-11T10:31:13-08:00","id":1175214,"title":"","content":"The beast of a vampire in Frenzy can decide that what it wants is to humiliate someone to be satisfied, and it doesn't even has to involve violence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-12T11:42:13-08:00","id":1175522,"title":"","content":"Page 103 side bar<br /> <b><i>''a vampire\u2019s rational consciousness is no longer in control during frenzy''</i></b><br /> <br /> Page 104<br /> <b><i>''The Frenzy<br /> Upon entering frenzy, determine what the Beast wants. Does it want to escape? Does it want to punish the person who insulted his host? Does it want blood?''</i></b><br /> <br /> If you still want to add a social aspect to it I would recomend demonic possession videos for inspiration. You know tongue frenzy. Rather than logical wickedness, which shouldn't happen.<br /> <br /> Sorry for being out of topic, but its already awkward and inappropriate to talk about vampire in a werewolf forum.<br /> <br /> Appart from all of that, staking a werewolf to the heart sounds more like a game group fun matter than an actual problem of what effect it may have, the simple rule should be frenzy for self perservation, I think the ST of <b> Vitalis</b>, roleplayed it appropriately and made the werewolf go away after taking aggravated damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}